<title>USA: GeoTel Communications ups IPO price range.</title>
<headline>GeoTel Communications ups IPO price range.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>GeoTel Communications Inc raised the estimated price tag for its shares in the company's proposed initial public offering to $11 to $12 each, according to underwriter Alex. Brown &amp; Sons Inc.</p>
<p>The Littleton, Massachussetts company had previously filed to offer shares in a range of $8 to $9 each. The number of shares remains the same, 2.2 million. They are to trade on the Nasdaq under the symbol &quot;GEOC&quot;.</p>
<p>The offering is expected to price tonight for trading tomorrow. GeoTel develops telecommunications software.</p>
</text>
